From 43286534f0454c7e85e9240c9f6517173c616872 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stuart0808 <20211402@bjtu.edu.cn>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:49:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] The front end builds the condition and the body of a loop
 as regions

A loop is written the way a branch is: its condition and its body are regions of the current
graph, built where they are written (Builder::buildArm with the kind LoopCond or LoopBody), their
ports are Port nodes of the region declared in its scope, and what the code names is read where
it is. The LOOP node gets the results of the parts and a round counter as With inputs. There is
no capture table of a loop any more (captureTwins_, buildLoopGraph, the loop graphs and their
names are gone), the program is not regionized after the front end, and the encoder, the
reachability walk, the effect analysis and the debug dump know the regions.

With the loop lowering gone from every back end, what only it used goes too:
loop_lowering, the hidden operators :loop/collector and :loop/collect, :graph/original and
Program::original. The facts test pass tallies the outlined program instead of the lowered one.
Two details found on the way: a loop's ports are nodes of its regions, and the layout of a loop
leaves the ctrl inputs that come from inside the loop to the regions.

